  <prompt>Add two new single-surface `kind:'workspace-tab'` entries to `surfaceLaunchRegistry` (Daily Briefing, Smart To Do) so the FR-06 follow-on cards (task 023) have launch targets. The registry is keyed by consumerType (one entry → one surface); the `list-tasks` entry (~:147) is the `kind:'workspace-tab'` precedent to follow. `handleSurfaceLaunch` (`ConversationPane.tsx` ~:1245–1312) already dispatches any workspace-tab/layout entry generically via PaneEventBus `widget_load` — do NOT add a code branch. No registry shape change (single-surface, per owner decision — no multi-surface fan-out).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer. React 18 + shared-lib expertise; comfortable with the surfaceHandoff `surfaceLaunchRegistry` contract, the consumerType → single-surface lookup, and the generic `handleSurfaceLaunch` workspace-tab dispatch via PaneEventBus `widget_load`.</role>
  <goal>Two new single-surface `kind:'workspace-tab'` registry entries (Daily Briefing, Smart To Do) exist and resolve via `resolveSurfaceLaunch`, so FR-06 follow-on cards have launch targets — with `handleSurfaceLaunch` dispatching them generically and no code branch added.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-06 launch targets. The `surfaceLaunchRegistry` (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/surfaceHandoff/surfaceLaunchRegistry.ts`) is keyed by consumerType, one entry → one surface. The `list-tasks` entry (~:147) is the shipped `kind:'workspace-tab'` precedent: it names a workspace widget `surface` (widget type), a `title`, and optional `widgetData`, and `handleSurfaceLaunch` (`ConversationPane.tsx` ~:1245–1312) dispatches ANY workspace-tab/layout entry generically via PaneEventBus `widget_load` — no per-entry code branch. This task adds two sibling entries following that precedent so the FR-06 follow-on cards (task 023) can open the Daily Briefing and Smart To Do tabs. Owner decision (spec Out of Scope): NO `surfaceLaunchRegistry` shape change and NO multi-surface launch fan-out — these are two individual single-surface entries. This task is additive config only; task 023 renders and gates the cards that dispatch these entries.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/surfaceHandoff/surfaceLaunchRegistry.ts (add the two entries; the list-tasks entry ~:147 is the kind:'workspace-tab' precedent)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (handleSurfaceLaunch ~:1245–1312 — the generic workspace-tab dispatcher; verify no branch needed)</file>
      <file>the registered workspace widget types for Daily Briefing + Smart To Do (the `surface`/widget-type values the two entries point at)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project" scope="the two registry entries">Add exactly two single-surface `kind:'workspace-tab'` entries (Daily Briefing, Smart To Do) following the `list-tasks` precedent; MUST NOT change the registry shape and MUST NOT introduce a multi-surface fan-out (owner Out-of-Scope decision).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="handleSurfaceLaunch">Reuse the generic workspace-tab dispatch — MUST NOT add a code branch to `handleSurfaceLaunch` (it already dispatches workspace-tab/layout entries generically via PaneEventBus `widget_load`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021" scope="any styling touched">Fluent v9 tokens-only; host-agnostic shared component — additive config must not regress other surfaceLaunch consumers.</constraint>
  </constraints>
